[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186316630 :answer-field/choices 17592186316403] [:db/retract 17592186316832 :answer-field/choices 17592186316280] [:db/retract 17592186316880 :answer-field/choices 17592186315550] [:db/retract 17592186316997 :answer-field/choices 17592186315151] [:db/retract 17592186316776 :answer-field/choices 17592186316223] {:db/id 17592186221449 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" "question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221451 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/id #uuid "6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-342257" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/64/64b557365c3642ae7a4206794080804bf2bbccb07230dfa46a4f415570f85329.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}-5x=-5(-2)=10\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}(2)^{2}=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd37979eada411b68755dfa85ec3b1e22585df2bff5c4bdd4b27cf06463706d6.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" "answer-field-dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" "answer-field-e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" "answer-field-c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7c63119-6c8c-562e-abc9-23fca39a632c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" :answer/id #uuid "6dac34b7-0afe-57b3-92dd-0f1fe22e6081" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/id #uuid "4dc4a3af-4483-521b-bb70-d53ecf298569" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" :answer/id #uuid "25e88e23-60be-52a5-b776-49ba011dac2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer/id #uuid "ae9e632a-9e59-5e68-bbaf-7f55bdadec72" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" :answer/id #uuid "5e730ffa-3f8d-587a-90e9-54ce2eab4291" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer/id #uuid "c97a6594-ee59-51ba-bb03-4d481212136d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer-field/choices ["answer-80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" :answer/id #uuid "80ea76ea-89c9-5952-ae08-cee6ace28d82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer/id #uuid "ee7734d0-53ef-5456-8980-faad9723c723" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317256 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316630 :answer-field/correct 17592186315456 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316832 :answer-field/correct 17592186316254 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316880 :answer-field/correct 17592186315605 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316997 :answer-field/correct 17592186315979 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222026 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & x\\in [0,1) \\\\ x, & x\\in [-1,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-1,1).$ \nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2e/2eb2120db83d33d37f1d076f7e3664a21cd1bb97ccd04aeb792cd8e510edf846.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}x=-1\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}1=1.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $2$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c91cf3eea948fdce9a992c77d95bc3c8bc5165ade9e6f17ae5b7e699b0a9be9d.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220836 :answer-field/correct 17592186220838 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220839 :answer-field/correct 17592186220841 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220833 :answer-field/correct 17592186220834 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220830 :answer-field/correct 17592186220831 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/id #uuid "e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342492" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+1, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ {x}^{2}+1, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/66/66b91f732d36469ded18df5404b3f12dddad7474168efd47ddf038835b67b831.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(-2x+1)=-2(-3)+1=7\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}({x}^{2}+1)=(3)^{2}+1=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/88/888053858d845bd47a56b953a5eb9a6f7f6b4ddffc0ecc70fa280e1a7d543f24.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" "answer-field-56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" "answer-field-37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" "answer-field-c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/id #uuid "ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/id #uuid "ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" :answer-field/id #uuid "56723ba2-cf0d-57bb-8655-32504888775c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" :answer/id #uuid "2c1a0160-ca7d-5739-9abb-99203387c9b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer/id #uuid "c4ef0c6d-3fca-5c4f-88d3-d5d53bd3106c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" :answer-field/id #uuid "37dba421-36d3-5977-b5b1-852f9e3aa421" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" "answer-733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer/id #uuid "64a4d026-4e1a-5cce-880b-42dd87fa4270" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0" :answer/id #uuid "733c52bb-6afa-5bc5-95c0-a7e66333b6e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c454f910-39f4-514e-b488-5dfacc09ef1d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" "answer-5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer/id #uuid "82fb8f4e-8153-5912-b8f4-8e162eb48f70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "False" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977" :answer/id #uuid "5f06001d-c0a8-5110-aaab-05496df93977" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "True" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/id #uuid "ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343391" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=3{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)={x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ \nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}({\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nt))\\text{d}t \\\\ [{t}^{3}]_{0}^{x} & ∼[{\\pi }^{2}t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nt)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ {x}^{3} & ∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" "answer-field-69166540-ccfc-5316-bfb5-4b3fcfefdc9f" "answer-field-07ef0176-9972-561f-b028-e97ddd2d78db" "answer-field-830beb7c-054e-556c-a7b8-6c335f330299"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/id #uuid "b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" "answer-b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" "answer-b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" "answer-44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" "answer-18700c44-863c-5283-8d80-b4ecba9f9a9b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/id #uuid "d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" :answer/id #uuid "b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/id #uuid "b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/id #uuid "b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" :answer/id #uuid "44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-