 :question/answer-fields "answer-field-dcc6415d-3e4e-531f-9f82-1e1222466f88"] ["question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e6e854c4-06f2-5c3a-8345-9858abe5cb7f"] ["question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c9e2bd45-2176-5d0a-8daf-b4630614c646"] [17592186221449 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6acce05c-927e-54a3-ab7e-dea3332ed930"] [17592186317256 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x\\in [-2,0) \\\\ -2, & x\\in [0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |"] [17592186316630 :answer-field/correct 17592186315456] [17592186316832 :answer-field/correct 17592186316254] [17592186316880 :answer-field/correct 17592186315605] [17592186316997 :answer-field/correct 17592186315979] [17592186222026 :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & x\\in [0,1) \\\\ x, & x\\in [-1,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-1,1).$ \nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |"] [17592186222026 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/2e/2eb2120db83d33d37f1d076f7e3664a21cd1bb97ccd04aeb792cd8e510edf846.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-1,1).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}x=-1\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}1=1.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and III are false.\n\n**Note:** The $2$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c91cf3eea948fdce9a992c77d95bc3c8bc5165ade9e6f17ae5b7e699b0a9be9d.png)"] [17592186222026 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186220836 :answer-field/correct 17592186220838] [17592186220839 :answer-field/correct 17592186220841] [17592186220833 :answer-field/correct 17592186220834] [17592186220830 :answer-field/correct 17592186220831] ["question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/id #uuid "e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d"] ["question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342492"] ["question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+1, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ {x}^{2}+1, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |"] ["question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/66/66b91f732d36469ded18df5404b3f12dddad7474168efd47ddf038835b67b831.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(-2x+1)=-2(-3)+1=7\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}({x}^{2}+1)=(3)^{2}+1=10.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement III is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/88/888053858d845bd47a56b953a5eb9a6f7f6b4ddffc0ecc70fa280e1a7d543f24.png)"] ["question-e3e7079a-616c-59e7-8130-14cd0fb2782d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/id #uuid "69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb"] ["answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/id #uuid "ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52"] ["answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52" :answer/value "False"] ["answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/id #uuid "ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51"] ["answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51" :answer/value "True"] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/correct "answer-ae6c9b1a-0549-532b-b72f-ea08c4affb51"] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :answer-field/choices "answer-ae29e0f7-ed28-5cbf-85ca-f73138f17f52"] ["answer-field-69e99acf-1398-5692-8061-029fa2a74beb" :an